WEBVTT

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:26.210
ashita he tsuzuku sakamichi no tochuu de

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:26.210
On the uphill road that leads to tomorrow

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:32.510
surechigau otona tachi wa tsubuyaku no sa

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:32.510
We pass by adults who tell us this

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.640
"ai toka yume toka risou mo wakaru kedo

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.640
"I can understand ideals such as love and dreams

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:43.810
me no mae no genjitsu wa sonna ni amaku nai" tte

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:43.810
but the real world isn't as easy as you think"

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:50.150
tsumazuki nagara mo korogari nagara mo

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:50.150
Even though we keep tripping and falling

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:55.360
kasabuta darake no jyounetsu wo wasuretaku nai

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:55.360
We have to remember these pains of growing up

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:58.830
otona ni narenai bokura no

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:58.830
For all of us who can't force ourselves to do so yet

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.330
tsuyogari wo hitotsu kiite kure

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.330
Listen to this one thing I have to say

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:04.540
nige mo kakure mo shinai kara

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:04.540
I won't run or cower away

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:07.460
waraitai yatsu dake warae

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:07.460
So whoever wants to laugh at me, go ahead

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:10.250
semete tayori nai bokura no

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:10.250
Since we can't be relied upon yet

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:12.800
jiyuu no me wo tsumitoranai de

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:12.800
Don't take away our seed of freedom

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:15.800
mizu wo ageru sono yakume wo

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:15.800
The task of nurturing this plant

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:18.890
hataseba iindarou?

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:18.890
That's all we have to do, right?

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:30.020
{Intro}

00:01:32.230 --> 00:01:34.440
The second spell, Rashirudo...

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:39.200
Just when I thought I could
finally read the next page...

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:42.120
What the hell is this second
spell supposed to be?

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:44.660
Is it a lightning spell
stronger than Zakeru?

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:55.920
This isn't good...

00:01:56.260 --> 00:01:57.550
What should I do?

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:58.760
This book...

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:01.550
What are you thinking about, Kiyomaro?

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:09.020
{Part A}

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:17.530
The Second Spell, Rashirudo!

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:22.410
Why the hell are you running around
naked this early in the morning?

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:23.910
What are you saying?

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:27.160
It's normal to change your
clothes in the morning.

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:30.330
But it doesn't mean that you have
to change on top of my desk...

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:32.380
Okay, let's go, Kiyomaro!

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:36.590
And where do you plan on going?

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:39.720
It's exactly what it looks like.
We're going to school.

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:41.090
Don't follow me.

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:45.010
Don't follow me!

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:49.020
But... as your instructor, I...

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:51.770
Whatever. Just stay home.

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:58.990
Please, Kiyomaro, let me
go to school with you!

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:00.320
You're annoying me!

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:01.870
Let go of my leg!

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:05.240
If you're not here, what
am I supposed to do?

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:09.750
You can go to the park, watch TV,
or do whatever you want!

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:12.170
Kiyomaro!

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:15.550
Kiyomaro, are you telling
me to play by myself?

00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:17.380
That's so cold!

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:20.010
Okay, shut up...

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:24.430
Okay, a friend, eh? You just
need to 'make' a friend?

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:26.310
Wait a second...

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:31.270
Vulcan

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:31.270
Here it is!
Your friend, Vulcan 300.

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:38.230
Vulcan! Vulcan!

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:41.530
Vulcan! My friend, Vulcan!

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:46.240
Aren't you lucky, Gash...
Nobody else has a friend like that.

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:47.910
Kiyomaro, thank you so much!

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:49.700
How old is Vulcan?

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:50.710
5 minutes.

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:52.870
What is Vulcan?

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:56.420
He's a robot that can launch
up to 300 air missiles.

00:03:56.420 --> 00:04:02.380
Vulcan

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:58.420
box of treats

00:03:57.130 --> 00:04:02.090
He has a Hyper Body made out
of a candy box and chopsticks.

00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:00.420
split chopsticks

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:02.380
Hyper body

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:06.050
Yes, Vulcan!
From now on, we're friends!

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:07.760
Let's play!

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:13.350
Vulcan, let's play! Let's play!

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:11.020
Aren't you lucky, Gash...

00:04:11.020 --> 00:04:12.810
I'm going to school. Bye!

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:31.040
What the...
What's with this atmosphere?

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:35.380
Hey, Kiyomaro, isn't everyone
acting a little strange?

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:37.290
Why did you follow me?

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:40.510
Weren't you playing with Vulcan? Hey!

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:44.970
No, I thought I would introduce
Vulcan to Suzume-dono.

00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:50.470
Just get in!

00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:52.640
Kiyomaro!

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:54.440
Good morning!

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:03.990
It's the same here...

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:16.500
But... aren't they acting a little weird?

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:26.550
So, you've got guts after all.

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:31.220
Takamine-kun!

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:33.640
It's amazing! Look!

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:35.060
This is big news!

00:05:41.570 --> 00:05:45.320
Oh, yeah. Yesterday's incident...
It's in the newspaper?

00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:46.450
That's why...

00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:49.240
Oh... when did they take that picture?

00:05:50.030 --> 00:05:51.620
I thought I just heard a voice...

00:05:52.540 --> 00:05:54.160
No, it was nothing.

00:05:57.040 --> 00:06:00.750
Oh, yeah. Mariko-chan and her friends
want to ask you something.

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:04.630
- Takamine-kun, is that okay?
- S-Sure...

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:07.760
The suspect had a gun, right?

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:11.220
Yeah, he had some kind of rifle.

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:15.480
Weren't you scared?

00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:18.560
I got goose bumps from
just watching it on TV.

00:06:18.850 --> 00:06:22.230
Well, you know...

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:35.750
That's amazing!

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:45.340
Quit fooling around!

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:48.260
Have you guys forgotten already?

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:53.010
He's a shady genius bastard
that barely comes to school!

00:06:53.350 --> 00:06:56.270
He's trying to act all nice now,
but the truth is...

00:06:56.270 --> 00:06:57.680
What are you saying?

00:06:57.680 --> 00:07:02.270
You're the bad guy here, but you're trying
to make Kiyomaro look like the bad guy!

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:07.940
You... You're the little punk from before!

00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:09.610
Aww, he's so cute!

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:10.990
Who is that little kid?

00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:12.740
Takamine-kun's little brother?

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:13.910
Bastard!

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:17.950
Where did your flying friend go?

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:20.580
I want to get revenge...

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:24.670
A flying friend, huh?

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:27.300
What nonsense are you
talking about, Kaneyama?

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:32.140
All right, first period is going to start now.

00:07:32.140 --> 00:07:33.510
Yes...

00:07:34.970 --> 00:07:38.220
Takamine... you did well.

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:42.940
But anyway...

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:48.990
I'm going to have to bring this kid to the infirmary
for supervision until lunch time.

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:52.410
Kiyomaro!

00:07:52.950 --> 00:07:54.530
It's your own fault...

00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:57.240
Okay, I'm going to take the attendance.

00:07:57.240 --> 00:07:58.580
- Ane?
- Here!

00:07:58.790 --> 00:08:00.540
- Inoue?
- Here!

00:08:00.870 --> 00:08:02.710
- Ishikawa?
- Here!

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:05.540
Infirmary

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:17.680
Today was pretty amazing.

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:20.350
Everyone wanted to talk to you.

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:22.520
It was all in their own self-interest.

00:08:24.940 --> 00:08:25.980
No, it's not!

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:29.150
Everyone finally noticed
your good qualities.

00:08:29.150 --> 00:08:30.900
I wonder...

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:32.110
It's true.

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:34.820
Hey, Gash-kun...

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:40.790
You know what... Ever since you came,
Takamine-kun has become really cool.

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:42.710
Of course!

00:08:42.710 --> 00:08:45.000
I'm always with him!

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:49.340
Please take care of
Takamine-kun from now on, too.

00:08:49.340 --> 00:08:51.010
Yes, leave it to me!

00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:53.090
What are you guys whispering about?

00:08:58.050 --> 00:08:59.390
It's a secret.

00:08:59.510 --> 00:09:01.060
S-e-c-r-e-t.

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:03.640
Well, see you tomorrow, Takamine-kun!

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:05.520
Farewell, Suzume-dono!

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:11.610
Suzume-dono is a great person.

00:09:11.610 --> 00:09:12.690
Yeah.

00:09:16.820 --> 00:09:18.160
Hey, Gash...

00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:20.700
What?

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:23.120
What is it, Kiyomaro?

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:24.910
Umm...

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:27.580
Thank...

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:29.630
Huh?

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:32.960
Well, whatever. I'll
eventually return the favor.

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:34.130
Gikoru!

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:42.640
W-What the...?

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:48.270
T-That's...

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:54.900
The guy from yesterday!

00:09:54.900 --> 00:09:58.240
Don't worry,
we're not after you.

00:09:58.490 --> 00:09:59.780
It's that kid.

00:10:14.050 --> 00:10:14.090
{Part B}

00:10:23.890 --> 00:10:27.230
Hand over that Gash kid
or whatever you call him.

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:29.480
Who would hand him over?

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:31.560
Who the hell would get handed over?

00:10:32.440 --> 00:10:35.900
Okay, then I'll have to take him by force.

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:38.200
Kiyomaro, leave it to me.

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:39.410
What?

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:43.330
With his Valivashi Bombardment,
Vulcan will blow him to bits!

00:10:46.540 --> 00:10:49.870
Stop saying stupid things, and go away!

00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:52.250
Gikoru!

00:10:54.590 --> 00:10:57.170
That move can come out
of the ground, too?

00:10:59.630 --> 00:11:02.430
It's just as I thought.
That kid is similar to Gash.

00:11:02.430 --> 00:11:05.140
Where did you find that kid?

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:06.430
I picked him up.

00:11:06.430 --> 00:11:08.730
Didn't you do the same thing?

00:11:08.730 --> 00:11:11.350
You're using him for
your own personal gain.

00:11:11.350 --> 00:11:12.560
My personal gain?

00:11:12.560 --> 00:11:13.900
Misoshiru?

00:11:12.560 --> 00:11:16.780
Misoshiru is miso soup. "Umai shiru" means good soup,
but in this context, it's referring to use for personal gain.

00:11:14.650 --> 00:11:15.780
No.

00:11:15.780 --> 00:11:17.190
Then it's tonjiru!

00:11:16.780 --> 00:11:19.740
Tonjiru is pork and vegetable soup.

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:18.190
No!

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:19.200
Kenchi-

00:11:19.650 --> 00:11:21.990
What kind of soup is it then?

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:24.740
Anyway, you're hitting
me too much, Kiyomaro!

00:11:24.740 --> 00:11:26.040
My bad.

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:29.910
After yesterday's bank
incident, I had doubts...

00:11:29.910 --> 00:11:32.500
But it looks like you just
started using the book.

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:35.540
All right, I'll tell you.

00:11:36.750 --> 00:11:40.970
When I found him, I was transporting
something and went into a warehouse.

00:11:44.260 --> 00:11:49.100
Inside the warehouse, this kid was busy
munching away on some frozen fish.

00:11:50.600 --> 00:11:53.150
Hey, what are you doing?

00:11:53.150 --> 00:11:56.570
If you eat this stuff without permission,
you're going to get into trouble.

00:12:04.570 --> 00:12:06.410
What's with this kid?

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:07.830
And from then on,

00:12:07.830 --> 00:12:11.710
no matter how many times I
tried to get rid of him, he kept on following me.

00:12:11.710 --> 00:12:12.920
And then...

00:12:12.920 --> 00:12:15.460
Stop messing around!
Damn it!

00:12:15.670 --> 00:12:22.430
I've been hungry, working on a low salary,
and because of one mistake, I get fired?

00:12:22.430 --> 00:12:24.760
Damn it! Mocking me like this...

00:12:25.340 --> 00:12:26.390
Hey.

00:12:26.390 --> 00:12:27.720
What do you want, kid?

00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:29.520
Try to read this book.

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:38.110
What's with these characters?

00:12:38.110 --> 00:12:39.780
I can't read this...

00:12:41.490 --> 00:12:43.450
Different colored characters...

00:12:43.450 --> 00:12:45.200
Gikoru...

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:47.120
Say it louder!

00:12:48.530 --> 00:12:49.990
All right, I'll read it!

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:52.370
You little shit, mocking me, too...

00:12:53.620 --> 00:12:54.790
Gikoru!

00:12:57.290 --> 00:12:59.420
Are you happy now?

00:13:09.560 --> 00:13:11.060
You...

00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:15.190
And from then on, I started my revenge.

00:13:16.310 --> 00:13:19.150
I sent the guy who fired me
to the hospital.

00:13:20.110 --> 00:13:24.740
And then, as revenge for being poor,
I robbed banks and jewelry stores.

00:13:25.650 --> 00:13:27.660
I did everything!

00:13:29.830 --> 00:13:32.080
I'm invincible with this power.

00:13:32.080 --> 00:13:33.660
What do you mean by invincible?

00:13:33.660 --> 00:13:36.330
Yesterday, Kiyomaro
totally defeated you!

00:13:36.870 --> 00:13:39.750
Yeah, that's why I'm going to take you.

00:13:41.170 --> 00:13:46.760
Did you know? This book reacts to your
hatred, anger, and even your desire.

00:13:47.050 --> 00:13:49.470
"I want money."
"I hate that guy."

00:13:49.470 --> 00:13:53.810
The stronger your feelings are,
the stronger the power is!

00:13:54.390 --> 00:13:57.770
This kid alone can't
fulfill my needs anymore.

00:13:58.270 --> 00:14:00.980
That's why I came to get that kid.

00:14:01.860 --> 00:14:04.400
Now that you know, hurry up
and give me that kid.

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:05.610
Listen.

00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:08.910
It's quite clear to me now
that you're a shit head.

00:14:09.410 --> 00:14:14.790
You use that kid to get money. You wear
nice clothes, and even jewelry.

00:14:15.370 --> 00:14:21.590
Yet, why is that kid wearing
dirty, torn clothes?

00:14:25.340 --> 00:14:27.760
And I was wondering what
you were going to say...

00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:33.890
This kid is a tool to fulfill my dreams.

00:14:36.020 --> 00:14:39.480
Why should I buy new clothes for a tool?

00:14:42.690 --> 00:14:45.440
Stop messing around!

00:14:47.190 --> 00:14:49.030
I won't forgive him either.

00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:51.160
Kiyomaro, let's beat him!

00:14:51.160 --> 00:14:52.370
Yeah!

00:14:53.080 --> 00:14:55.040
What are you getting all worked up for?

00:14:55.040 --> 00:14:56.750
Zakeru!

00:14:57.910 --> 00:14:59.250
Gikoru!

00:15:06.090 --> 00:15:07.090
Gikoru!

00:15:10.180 --> 00:15:11.590
Don't underestimate us!

00:15:11.590 --> 00:15:13.640
No matter how many times you use that...

00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:14.850
Furizudo!

00:15:21.400 --> 00:15:22.730
Kiyomaro!

00:15:23.730 --> 00:15:24.940
Kiyomaro...

00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:28.070
Are you trying to say this kid is human?

00:15:28.070 --> 00:15:32.200
Stop joking around. How would a human
child have this kind of power?

00:15:32.490 --> 00:15:34.660
This kid is a monster!

00:15:35.990 --> 00:15:39.620
And a very useful monster
that listens to me, to boot.

00:15:39.910 --> 00:15:42.170
You bastard. Stop...

00:15:42.170 --> 00:15:43.210
Whoops.

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:47.840
So this is your tool and your book.

00:15:48.510 --> 00:15:52.890
This is perfect. I'll test
him out by killing you.

00:15:54.140 --> 00:15:55.720
Okay...

00:15:57.850 --> 00:15:59.480
I can't read this at all.

00:16:00.270 --> 00:16:05.230
I get it. Even if he can read the blue book, it
doesn't mean that he can read the red one.

00:16:05.690 --> 00:16:07.730
It means one can't read another's book.

00:16:08.730 --> 00:16:11.490
As I recall, you said
something like "Zakeru."

00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:21.710
Zakeru!

00:16:29.210 --> 00:16:32.010
Stop fooling around! Why
isn't it coming out?

00:16:32.010 --> 00:16:33.550
You useless piece of shit!

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:35.050
Gash!

00:16:36.720 --> 00:16:38.100
You bastard...

00:16:38.100 --> 00:16:41.140
Tools should just act like tools,
and listen to what I say!

00:16:42.390 --> 00:16:44.270
Gash, run away!

00:16:45.150 --> 00:16:47.480
That's enough. Run away, now!

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:52.990
This tool dares to talk
back to me. How naive...

00:16:54.660 --> 00:16:59.080
If you keep insulting me,
I won't forgive you!

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:04.370
Yes!

00:17:04.370 --> 00:17:07.960
I see. You've grown stronger
since that bank robbery.

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:12.720
Good job. Good job, Gash!

00:17:12.720 --> 00:17:13.920
Kiyomaro...

00:17:14.470 --> 00:17:17.430
I hit him once.

00:17:17.850 --> 00:17:19.890
Yeah, good job.

00:17:20.310 --> 00:17:23.180
Damn it... How dare you
mess around with me.

00:17:23.930 --> 00:17:27.400
I don't need that kid anymore.
I'm going to kill both of you!

00:17:28.020 --> 00:17:29.110
This isn't good.

00:17:29.110 --> 00:17:31.360
Gash, look at this ice.

00:17:34.070 --> 00:17:38.370
I have to destroy only the ice. I need
to focus my mind. "I hate the ice."

00:17:38.370 --> 00:17:39.580
Die!

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:43.040
I hate this ice that binds me!

00:17:43.410 --> 00:17:44.620
Gikoru!

00:17:51.920 --> 00:17:53.880
You made me waste so much time...

00:17:54.590 --> 00:17:55.800
Zakeru!

00:17:55.800 --> 00:17:56.800
What?

00:17:57.890 --> 00:17:59.430
Gikoru!

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:04.730
You bastard. Stop it already.

00:18:04.810 --> 00:18:07.270
Now you're using that kid as a shield?

00:18:09.520 --> 00:18:11.730
Hey, you. Just stop it.

00:18:12.400 --> 00:18:14.690
Why are you letting that guy use you?

00:18:14.690 --> 00:18:17.700
Aren't you sad that he's
using you as he wishes?

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:22.240
You've misunderstood something.

00:18:22.240 --> 00:18:23.330
What?

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:28.500
The more this guy uses
me, the stronger I get.

00:18:28.670 --> 00:18:34.880
And his becoming more evil brings me more
pleasure than anything in this world.

00:18:35.800 --> 00:18:38.840
So this kid actually chose this guy?

00:18:39.430 --> 00:18:40.840
That's how it is...

00:18:41.720 --> 00:18:43.100
Let's do it, Reikomu.

00:18:43.100 --> 00:18:44.430
All right, Hosokawa.

00:18:44.520 --> 00:18:45.970
Let's destroy them.

00:18:46.600 --> 00:18:49.230
Kiyomaro, don't get distracted.

00:18:49.310 --> 00:18:51.020
You must not lose your feelings.

00:18:51.110 --> 00:18:52.650
Yeah, it's going to be all right.

00:18:52.980 --> 00:18:54.150
Furizudo!

00:18:58.110 --> 00:19:00.820
They're on a completely
different level, after all...

00:19:00.820 --> 00:19:05.660
I can't even run. What should I do?
There has to be another way...

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:10.370
The book... level?

00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:13.090
That's right, I forgot!

00:19:13.090 --> 00:19:17.630
This book has changed as well.
I, too, have a trump card!

00:19:18.670 --> 00:19:20.760
It looks like this is the end.

00:19:21.550 --> 00:19:24.390
I don't know if this is
going to be good or bad,

00:19:24.390 --> 00:19:25.390
but...

00:19:25.720 --> 00:19:27.680
This is the end!

00:19:27.680 --> 00:19:31.020
There's still a chance that I can beat you!

00:19:31.270 --> 00:19:32.600
Gikoru!

00:19:35.860 --> 00:19:37.230
Rashirudo!

00:19:41.410 --> 00:19:44.410
Is it a shield? Wait,
there's something more...

00:19:50.960 --> 00:19:53.710
N-No way...

00:19:59.260 --> 00:20:03.430
Wow, what a spell. It reflected
their spell right back at them,

00:20:03.930 --> 00:20:06.720
and even added some lightning to it.

00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:14.350
Hey, are you all right?

00:20:23.860 --> 00:20:25.870
Idiot, you're going to burn yourself!

00:20:26.410 --> 00:20:28.240
It's not going out!

00:20:28.990 --> 00:20:31.750
His blue book is burning...

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:36.670
His body is disappearing...

00:20:37.210 --> 00:20:38.340
H-Hey, wait!

00:20:38.590 --> 00:20:40.010
Y-You...

00:20:42.840 --> 00:20:46.140
N-No way... Reikomu...

00:20:51.140 --> 00:20:54.140
After the book burned up,
the kid disappeared...

00:21:05.070 --> 00:21:05.110
{Ending}

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:20.840
ne konna koto tsuzukete itemo

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:20.840
You know, even if we continue to progress like this

00:21:21.380 --> 00:21:26.050
shiawase wa mitsukaru no kana?

00:21:21.380 --> 00:21:26.050
Will we be able to find true happiness?

00:21:26.720 --> 00:21:31.180
tarinai mono kazoete mitemo

00:21:26.720 --> 00:21:31.180
When I try counting what is missing in my life

00:21:31.890 --> 00:21:36.310
kiri ga nai no wakatteru you

00:21:31.890 --> 00:21:36.310
I know the list will keep going on and on

00:21:36.810 --> 00:21:41.980
shinario douri nante

00:21:36.810 --> 00:21:41.980
Everything goes according to plans

00:21:42.280 --> 00:21:46.740
umaku iku wake nai kara

00:21:42.280 --> 00:21:46.740
Of course that can never happen

00:21:47.110 --> 00:21:49.370
toki ni wa zenbu

00:21:47.110 --> 00:21:49.370
At times, everything that I have

00:21:49.700 --> 00:21:52.200
nagedashi taku naru

00:21:49.700 --> 00:21:52.200
I just want to let it all go

00:21:52.660 --> 00:21:58.000
sonna hi ga attemo iiyone

00:21:52.660 --> 00:21:58.000
Is it uncommon to have days like this?

00:22:00.630 --> 00:22:05.550
hito wa mina okubyou dakara

00:22:00.630 --> 00:22:05.550
Everyone is afraid, even though we don't show it

00:22:05.760 --> 00:22:10.050
yume wo miru no kana?

00:22:05.760 --> 00:22:10.050
Is that why we dream?

00:22:10.970 --> 00:22:15.930
hito wa mina kodoku dakara

00:22:10.970 --> 00:22:15.930
Everyone feels lonely on the inside

00:22:16.140 --> 00:22:20.440
ai wo sagasu no kana?

00:22:16.140 --> 00:22:20.440
Is that why we look for love?

00:22:20.940 --> 00:22:23.440
kitto chigau

00:22:20.940 --> 00:22:23.440
Even though you are not here

00:22:23.610 --> 00:22:25.860
basho de kimi mo

00:22:23.610 --> 00:22:25.860
know that where ever you are

00:22:26.320 --> 00:22:28.030
onaji tsuki wo

00:22:26.320 --> 00:22:28.030
You are gazing up

00:22:28.240 --> 00:22:31.700
miteru you ne...

00:22:28.240 --> 00:22:31.700
at the same moon as me...

00:22:35.120 --> 00:22:35.160
{Preview}

00:22:38.080 --> 00:22:40.420
Kiyomaro, what exactly am I?

00:22:40.420 --> 00:22:41.790
Gash has finally realized...

00:22:41.790 --> 00:22:44.960
Lightning comes out of
my mouth, doesn't it?

00:22:45.300 --> 00:22:46.920
Am I better than a normal being?

00:22:46.920 --> 00:22:48.470
What are you thinking?

00:22:48.470 --> 00:22:51.300
If you make one mistake, you'll
become a tool for killing!

00:22:51.300 --> 00:22:55.220
So? It's too sad to be
known only as a monster...

00:22:55.770 --> 00:22:57.730
Next time on Konjiki no Gash Bell:

00:22:57.730 --> 00:23:00.060
The Battle Between 100 Demons.

00:23:00.060 --> 00:23:03.020
Two shadows are closing
in on the depressed Gash.

00:23:02.110 --> 00:23:05.070
The Battle Between 100 Demons
